WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.801
-Former president
and allegedly current

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:06.634
presidential candidate
Donald Trump, once again,

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:09.567
lost his mind in a series
of unhinged social media posts

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.601
as the district attorney
investigating his attempt

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:15.367
to overturn the election results
in Georgia revealed in court

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.133
that she's close
to announcing decisions

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:19.033
regarding possible indictments
in the case

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.400
and even suggested

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.701
that there could be more
than one defendant.

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:24.868
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:28.901
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:30.067
As you may recall,

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.434
in the days leading
up to the coup attempt

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:33.567
on January 6th,
Trump tried to pressure

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:36.434
Georgia's Republican secretary
of state, Brad Raffensperger,

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:39.067
to manipulate the vote tally
in Georgia

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:40.834
and overturn
Joe Biden's victory.

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:43.100
In particular,
there was that infamous line

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.567
where Trump just confessed

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:46.200
and told them
what he was asking for.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.033
He wanted them to magically find
enough votes for him to win.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:59.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:01.801
Trump has the same energy
attempting a coup

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.300
as someone who's been
on the phone

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.434
with Verizon customer service
for an hour.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:07.467
[ Laughter ]
"Look, all I want to do is this.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:10.200
I just want to find, uh...

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:12.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.267
Maybe Trump's pause was

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.133
because he didn't want
to sound suspicious,

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:18.434
asking for the exact amount
of votes he needed to win.

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:20.200
[ Laughter ]
He was trying to sound like it

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.200
was an arbitrary number
he pulled out of thin air.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.300
[ As Trump ]
Look, this isn't even
about winning or losing, for me.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.801
It's about getting
the count right

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:29.300
and, if we do that and Joe Biden
is still the winner,

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.067
I'll be the first
to congratulate him.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:32.367
So, I'll just come up
with a number

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:33.367
off the top of my head --

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:37.534
[ Laughter ]
11,780!

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:38.701
[ Applause ]

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:39.868
That's, of course,

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.801
the most infamous line
from the phone call,

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.100
but the parts that remain
truly astounding to me

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.667
are all the deranged
conspiracy theories

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:48.667
Trump unfurled over the course
of an hour-long rant,

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:50.300
including stuff he admitted,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.133
during the call,
may not be true.

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:54.701
Here are a few highlights,
in case you managed to block all

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:56.434
of this from your memory
and move on with your life,

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.300
in which case, congrats.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:11.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:24.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:37.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:56.234
Oof! It makes me feel bad
for Raffensperger.

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:57.934
He must've that same
feeling I get

00:02:57.934 --> 00:02:59.367
when I take an Uber
to the airport

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:01.734
and, within two minutes,
the driver locks eyes on me

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:04.501
in his rearview mirror and says,
"So, you uh,

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:05.968
ever listen to Alex Jones?"

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:09.100
There's so much to unpack here,

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.400
starting with Trump's insistence
that dead people are voting.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.334
Now, of course, what he means is
people use dead people's names

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:16.567
to fraudulently vote --
which also didn't happen --

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:19.167
but he's too scatterbrained
to explain it that way,

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:23.167
[ Laughter ]
so it just sounds like he thinks
an army of zombie Biden voters

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:24.767
[ Laughter ]
cost him the election.

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:26.000
Trump then went on to say this.

00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:49.734
[ Laughter ]
Anytime you say the words,
"This may or may not be true,"

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.534
[ Laughter ]
and those words
are immediately followed

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:54.667
by "They're burning ballots,"
it's definitely not true.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.033
[ Laughter ]
I mean, most of Trump's
conspiracy theories,

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:59.834
I can at least trace back
to some tiny kernel of truth

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:01.767
that his diseased mind
then twisted

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:03.267
into some elaborate fantasy,
but this one,

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:05.334
I honestly have no [bleep] clue
where he got it from.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.100
[ Laughter ]
And, interestingly,

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.267
we never heard about it again.

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:10.901
I mean, burning ballots?
Did he go to a magic show

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:12.534
and think it was
a polling place?

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:13.901
[ Laughter ]
[ As Trump ] You know,
they're burning the ballots

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:15.133
and then the ballots disappear.

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:17.267
They go poof, gone,
or so it seems.

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:19.334
[ Laughter ]
But then they pull the ballot
out of a hat

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:21.400
and you think,
"It can be the same ballot."

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.000
[ Laughter ]
But then, then they say,
"Is this your ballot?"

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.167
And, sure enough, it is.
It is your ballot.

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.234
[ Laughter ]
And then they take out
a big suitcase

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.734
and they stuff a lady into it
and they chop her in half.

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:33.133
[ Laughter ]
It's very sad.
They chop her in half

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:34.567
and then she gets
to vote twice --

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.434
once for the head
and once for the legs.

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:38.767
[ Laughter ]
Because, now, she's
legally two people,

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:40.667
two people who both vote
for Joe Biden,

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:42.734
which is very suspicious.

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:44.868
[ Laughter ]
Very suspicious and very sad.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:47.300
But also, can we can we go
back to this?

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:53.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:58.200
No, I can't believe that.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.801
[ Laughter and applause ]
Slow-motion instant replay

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:03.334
is such an old person way
of saying it.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:04.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.334 --> 00:05:05.901
Sounds like the name
of a segment

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:07.567
on "America's Funniest
Home Videos."

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:09.968
"Now, let's check out the
slow-motion instant replay

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:12.167
of Dad taking a soccer ball
in the groin.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:14.067
And, oh!
That's got to hurt!"

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:16.000
[ Laughter and applause ]
Now, in all fairness,

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.234
that's not the face Rudy makes
when he's hit in the balls.

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:20.501
That's the face he makes
every time he remembers that,

00:05:20.501 --> 00:05:22.133
by being
Donald Trump's attorney,

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:23.667
he's -- to use the legal term --

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:25.000
getting hit
in the balls every day.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.334
[ Laughter ]
For example,

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:28.567
the district attorney
in Fulton County, Fani Willis,

00:05:28.567 --> 00:05:30.267
has been investigating
this phone call

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:31.634
and the pressure campaign
around it,

00:05:31.634 --> 00:05:33.567
to the point where she's
subpoenaed, among others,

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:34.734
Senator Lindsey Graham;

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.334
former Trump campaign counsel
Jenna Ellis;

00:05:36.334 --> 00:05:37.501
and Rudy Giuliani.

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:39.601
In fact, Giuliani was informed,
last year,

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:41.167
that he's a target
of the investigation

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:43.033
and he was also called
to testify

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:44.467
before the grand jury in August.

00:05:44.467 --> 00:05:46.801
-President Trump's former
lawyer Rudy Giuliani

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:48.801
faced a grilling for six hours

00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:51.567
before a grand jury
in Atlanta yesterday.

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:55.334
Giuliani testifying as a target
of the criminal probe looking

00:05:55.334 --> 00:05:58.734
into possible 2020
election interference there.

00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:02.033
-We do know that it very likely
centered around statements

00:06:02.033 --> 00:06:05.133
that Giuliani made to Georgia
lawmakers back in 2020,

00:06:05.133 --> 00:06:07.467
just on the heels
of the presidential election,

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:10.200
where he came forth and made
a number of false claims

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.100
and, really, conspiracy theories

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.167
about the election here
in Georgia.

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:16.567
-What kind of charges,
potentially, would that mean?

00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:20.934
-You know, the DA here
in Fulton County has indicated

00:06:20.934 --> 00:06:24.033
that this could lead
to possible charges ranging

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:26.667
from racketeering
to possible conspiracy charges.

00:06:26.667 --> 00:06:28.868
-Racketeering makes sense.
Conspiracy does, too,

00:06:28.868 --> 00:06:30.734
but it might be a harder sell
to a jury

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:32.534
because Rudy is so bad
at conspiracy.

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:35.467
He literally holds up
incriminating texts on TV.

00:06:35.467 --> 00:06:38.033
[ Laughter ]
He meets with shady characters
in cigar bars

00:06:38.033 --> 00:06:39.667
and then takes pictures.

00:06:39.667 --> 00:06:41.667
[ As Giuliani ]
Remember, fellas,
we never had this conversation.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:44.334
Now, how about a quick picture,
so we never forget it?

00:06:44.334 --> 00:06:47.300
[ Laughter ]
Also, my sympathies
to the grand jury members

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.767
who had to sit there and listen
to Rudy Giuliani for six hours.

00:06:50.767 --> 00:06:52.801
And that probably feels like
12 hours to Rudy

00:06:52.801 --> 00:06:54.634
because, as we discovered
during a recent

00:06:54.634 --> 00:06:56.734
disciplinary hearing conducted
via Zoom,

00:06:56.734 --> 00:06:59.133
he sometimes wears two watches

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:00.300
by accident.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.067
[ Indistinct conversation ]

00:07:07.067 --> 00:07:08.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.834 --> 00:07:13.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:13.801 --> 00:07:16.567
I mean, if I'm Rudy's attorney,
that's my entire defense.

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:20.300
[ Laughter ]
I'll just let the prosecution go
for weeks on end,

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.801
building a case that my client
committed conspiracy.

00:07:22.801 --> 00:07:26.400
When it's my turn, I'd stand up,
face the jury, and say,

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.801
"He didn't know he had
two watches on.

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:31.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.567
Uh, the defense, uh, rests."

00:07:33.567 --> 00:07:35.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:36.934
So, that's where
the investigation stood

00:07:36.934 --> 00:07:39.234
until yesterday,
when Willis appeared in court

00:07:39.234 --> 00:07:41.767
for a hearing on whether to make
the grand jury's report public.

00:07:41.767 --> 00:07:44.734
Willis asked the judge to keep
the report private, for now,

00:07:44.734 --> 00:07:46.567
and she did so
for a tantalizing reason.

00:07:46.567 --> 00:07:49.167
She said she was
about to announce decisions

00:07:49.167 --> 00:07:51.067
about indictments in the case

00:07:51.067 --> 00:07:53.067
regarding multiple
potential defendants.

00:07:53.067 --> 00:07:54.901
-New tonight --
The district attorney

00:07:54.901 --> 00:07:58.234
in Fulton County, Georgia,
which includes much of Atlanta,

00:07:58.234 --> 00:08:00.534
says her decision on charges
in the probe

00:08:00.534 --> 00:08:03.000
of former President Trump's
efforts to overturn

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:06.300
the 2020 presidential election
is imminent.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:09.334
-Fulton County DA Fani Willis
has asked the judge

00:08:09.334 --> 00:08:12.000
to keep the report under seal,

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:14.601
citing concerns
for "future defendants."

00:08:14.601 --> 00:08:20.501
-We think, for future defendants
to be treated fairly,

00:08:20.501 --> 00:08:22.868
it's not appropriate,
at this time,

00:08:22.868 --> 00:08:24.901
to have this report released.

00:08:24.901 --> 00:08:28.300
We are asking that the report
not be released

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.300
because you haven't seen
that report.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.501
Decisions are imminent.

00:08:33.501 --> 00:08:34.934
-Now, I gave up,
a long time ago,

00:08:34.934 --> 00:08:36.801
predicting whether Trump
will ever be indicted,

00:08:36.801 --> 00:08:39.067
since he seems to wriggle
his way out of every jam

00:08:39.067 --> 00:08:40.601
he's ever been in,
which is surprising,

00:08:40.601 --> 00:08:41.934
given that he has
the flexibility

00:08:41.934 --> 00:08:44.200
of a Mr. Potato Head
that got dropped in the toilet.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:46.701
[ Laughter ]
I mean, look at him.
Why is he only capable

00:08:46.701 --> 00:08:48.100
of bending at the waist
like that?

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:49.534
[ Laughter ]

00:08:49.534 --> 00:08:51.701
He looks like one of those
drinking birds.

00:08:51.701 --> 00:08:53.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:53.934 --> 00:08:55.200
But I will say,
if there are going

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.767
to be any indictments
in this case, at all,

00:08:57.767 --> 00:09:00.434
you would assume that one
of them would be the guy

00:09:00.434 --> 00:09:02.767
who made the phone call,
unless, of course,

00:09:02.767 --> 00:09:05.200
Trump made a plea deal
and turned on Rudy.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:07.968
[ As Trump ]
It was Rudy's idea.
We were having a sleepover

00:09:07.968 --> 00:09:11.033
[ Laughter ]
and he said, "Let's do --
Let's do some prank calls."

00:09:11.033 --> 00:09:13.234
And I said, "I don't know, Rudy.
We might get in trouble."

00:09:13.234 --> 00:09:14.567
[ Applause ]
And he said,
"It'll be hilarious.

00:09:14.567 --> 00:09:17.534
Let's call Georgia and tell them
dead people are voting."

00:09:17.534 --> 00:09:18.567
[ Laughter ]

00:09:18.567 --> 00:09:19.701
He did all the talking.

00:09:19.701 --> 00:09:21.200
I just did background boos.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.534
[ Laughter ]
I did -- I did spooky noises.

00:09:23.534 --> 00:09:26.000
[ Laughter ]

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.434
Of course, Trump didn't make
a plea deal.

00:09:27.434 --> 00:09:30.000
In fact, the case sent him
into a tailspin and prompted him

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.934
to go nuts on his fake Twitter
rip-off, Truth Social.

00:09:32.934 --> 00:09:34.367
Trump wrote,
among other things...

00:09:37.701 --> 00:09:39.133
[ Laughter ]

00:09:52.634 --> 00:09:54.000
[ Laughter ]

00:10:00.067 --> 00:10:01.167
[ Laughter ]

00:10:04.167 --> 00:10:07.300
[ Laughter ]
I love that his argument is,
"If I was so crazy,

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:09.133
how come they didn't
hang up on me?"

00:10:09.133 --> 00:10:12.133
Because you were the [bleep]
president, dude!

00:10:12.133 --> 00:10:16.501
[ Laughter and applause ]
I know it's crazy,
but it fully happened.

00:10:16.501 --> 00:10:17.934
[ Laughter ]
But just because you
were president

00:10:17.934 --> 00:10:20.400
doesn't mean you were,
all of a sudden, making sense.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.033
You were just too important
to hang up on.

00:10:22.033 --> 00:10:23.434
If people could hang up
on the president,

00:10:23.434 --> 00:10:25.100
don't you think "Fox &amp; Friends"
would've done that

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.534
[ Laughter ]
during one of your rambling,
hour-long phone calls,

00:10:27.534 --> 00:10:29.367
instead of staring
at you dead-eyed,

00:10:29.367 --> 00:10:31.868
like tourists watching two rats
hump on the subway?

00:10:31.868 --> 00:10:33.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.434
Also, if they had
hung up on you,

00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:38.100
I'm pretty sure you would've
made a big deal about that, too.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:39.367
You don't strike me
as the type of guy

00:10:39.367 --> 00:10:41.567
who hears a sudden dial tone
and looks inward.

00:10:41.567 --> 00:10:44.634
[ English accent ]
Oh, dear! They've...
hung up on me. I...

00:10:44.634 --> 00:10:47.167
hope I didn't say anything
to offend.

00:10:47.167 --> 00:10:49.267
[ Laughter ]

00:10:49.267 --> 00:10:51.334
Also, they did tell you,
multiple times,

00:10:51.334 --> 00:10:52.734
on the call,
that you were wrong.

00:10:52.734 --> 00:10:55.200
In fact, my favorite example
of that was when Trump was asked

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.934
about some video he claimed
to have seen, supposedly showing

00:10:57.934 --> 00:11:01.000
that Biden ballots
were scanned more than once,

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:03.601
which prompted Raffensperger
to say he would send Trump

00:11:03.601 --> 00:11:06.367
a link to the real video
debunking Trump's claim.

00:11:19.567 --> 00:11:20.667
[ Laughter ]

00:11:33.434 --> 00:11:36.801
[ Laughter ]
-I ha-- Mr. President --

00:11:36.801 --> 00:11:38.567
[ Laughter ]
"I have a --

00:11:38.567 --> 00:11:39.767
I have a much better link"

00:11:39.767 --> 00:11:41.501
is such a snotty
little thing to say,

00:11:41.501 --> 00:11:43.367
while also fundamentally
misunderstanding

00:11:43.367 --> 00:11:45.000
the technology
of what a link is.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.334
[ Laughter and applause ]
Trump is not technologically
proficient.

00:11:47.334 --> 00:11:48.801
[ Laughter ]
Do you want the Wi-Fi password?

00:11:48.801 --> 00:11:51.667
[ As Trump ]
No. I've got my own Wi-Fi,
got my own links.

00:11:51.667 --> 00:11:53.634
[ Laughter ]

00:11:53.634 --> 00:11:56.634
Got my own Wi-Fi,
got a couple of loose URLs.

00:11:56.634 --> 00:11:58.767
We know what that stands for --
U R Losers.

00:11:58.767 --> 00:12:00.367
[ Laughter ]
